Hello All,

I hope you had a gReat summer! It's time for our weekly work group to restart. We will meet on Thursdays from 11am-1pm in the DataLab/DSI classroom (360 Shields Library). Our first meeting will be this Thursday, 09/26.

We have quite the line up for presentations this quarter! I am including the tentative schedule below. The schedule may shift based on pending presentations/presenters, so keep an eye out for changes if you're particularly interested in a given topic.

datetopic
26-SepUpdate Fest: Installing R, Rstudio, and updating packages
3-OctIntro to R: Vectors & Data Types
10-OctIntro to R: Subsetting Vectors
17-OctEvan Batzer on linear models in R
24-OctNo presentation
31-OctData Frames and Subsetting
7-NovAmy Collins on Google Earth Engine and other things
14-NovFactors
21-NovDplyr: Select, Filter, Mutate
27-NovThanksgiving; No working group
5-DecDplyr: group_by, summarize, arrange, count
12-DecIntro to ggplot2

Best,
Taylor

--
Taylor Reiter
PhD Candidate
Food Science Graduate Group
Lab for Data Intensive Biology
University of California, Davis

